{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1534172-true-fae-for-second-edition","id":1534172,"title":"True Fae for Second Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-13T17:18:01-07:00","id":1534172,"title":"True Fae for Second Edition","content":"I was wondering if someone would be willing to walk me through the creation process for a True Fae using second edition rules? I am mainly curious about the rules for names and titles. I am wondering if one is creating a Fae with multiple titles, do those titles have to follow a general theme? One of the Fae Keepers I have for four of my Changelings is based on Surtur from Norse Mythology and I have given him the Title of &quot;The Black Jarl of the Fiery Sword&quot;. The way I had originally designed him I broke him down into the following titles: The Black Jarl, Jarl of the Fiery Sword, and the Realm title of Muspelheim. I am wondering if I did this correctly if titles have to be separate and distinct from one another? For added Clarity I have included what I have written about him so far minus the stat block as I haven't figured that part out yet.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Cultural Inspiration: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Norse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Fae</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: The Black Jarl of the Fiery Sword (Comes Ater Ferri Igneum) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Name and Titles:</span></b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The Black Jarl (Comes Ater)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Jarl of the Fiery Sword (Comes Ferri Igneum)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Muspelheim (Mundus Ignis)</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Description: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">When the Black Jarl manifests himself in order to interact with his changelings he generally appears as a truly massive, powerfully built, gigantic male with a chiseled physique and skin composed of molten lava with a solidified, black surface crisscrossed with cracks and fissures allowing the fiery orange and yellow glow of the molten lava beneath to show through. When in this form his eyes and open mouth radiate a fiery glow from within. Occasionally, he may also choose to manifest as human of Scandinavian descent with a powerful build, chiseled physique, golden eyes, with long fiery red hair and a full beard. In this form his skin is covered in a thin layer of soot and is dressed as a Viking age blacksmith and warrior.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Heraldry Tincture Colors: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Warm Colors and Black</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Realm:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> As the Black Jarl is not only the ruler of the realm of Muspelheim, but also the realm itself; he deigns to manifest as a vast volcanic wasteland that is in a constant state of eruption. The realm is littered with grand lakes of lava constantly fed by myriad active volcanoes scattered throughout the domain. At its heart lies a grand fortress seemingly carved from the walls of the caldera of Muspelheim\u2019s largest volcano. It is within this fortress that the Black Jarl reigns. Not only are the various features of this fiery hellscape a manifestation of the Black Jarl, but so are a great many of its inhabitants. The inhabitants that populate his domain manifestation are inspired from the many mythological creatures of various human cultures with an affinity for fire, earth, or strength such as Salamanders and other elementals of fire, Oreads and other elementals of earth, as well as the Eldjotnar and Cyclopes of Norse and Greek Mythology. The fire and earth elementals, both manifestation and changeling, serve as forge fires and laborers respectively. The Eldjotnar and Cyclopes, both manifestation and changeling, on the other hand serve as metalsmiths, guards, and warriors. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Possible Seemings: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Elementals and Ogres</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Possible Kiths: </span></b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Artists</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Bright Ones</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Cyclopeans</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Delvers</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Ifrits</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Stoneflesh</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Escaped Changelings:</span></b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Wildfire Jack is an Elemental/Ifrit</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Stoneface Stacy is an Elemental/Stoneflesh</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Eldberg is an Ogre/Ifrit</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">One-Eyed Jack is an Ogre/Cyclopean</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Please let me know what you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T18:30:48-07:00","id":1534177,"title":"","content":"A Title is a character. It's conceivable that a Fae might put all their efforts toward aligning their Titles toward a specific theme, but the Name doesn't manifest unless the Fae has no Titles because a Title is like a combination stock portfolio and shell corporation, made more powerful by the Fae's overall holdings manifested through other Titles.<br /> <br /> They <i>could</i> put all their eggs in one basket and have one Title manifest as their castle, another as the king within the castle, and a third as the elite corps of knights that goes out into the world, and even make the effort to ensure that all three Titles fit a stones-and-gems motif (nobody's going to tell a godlike egomaniac how to spend their money), but since Titles are all that stand between a Fae and functional mortality just as many of them are going to express their all-consuming greed in more diversified fashion, particularly given that Regalia and pledgecraft give them substantial latitude in dealing with things that don't require direct manifestations of pseudodivine authority and power to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T07:44:28-07:00","id":1534194,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your help, Would it be better for the True Fae to limit his realm manifestation to a single Location within the realm, like a Fortress or Manor, rather than the entire realm itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}